## Re-verified against current source

- `StudyEngine.fs:337-356` `blackBoxShape` admits a fitted path only when it bears
  at most one unknown matrix (`oneUnknownMatrix`). AT-1's QZ-then-LR runs bear two,
  so `engineWith` returns `NonlinearStudyEngine`; `runFit` (`:1844-1848`) calls
  `fitNonlinear`, whose `derivedGainOpt` (`:426-438`) refuses any anchored or
  interpolated session gain. The measured error (log 40836) is exactly that refusal:
  `'LP-LP' anchors its gain to LP-(AIR#0)-LP-2, LP-(AIR#0)-LP-2R`.
- The linear engine already handles this shape: `objectSolvesWith` (`:1102-1157`)
  fits each lone object from its own runs and `solveSeries` reconstructs a series'
  combined matrix as a diagnostic, never as constituent coefficients. Selection is
  stricter than the engine it routes to; that inconsistency is the defect.
- The spec requires the fix, not a waiver: `.spec-md:373` chooses the engine by
  whether the unknowns enter linearly, and 001 §L (line 435) lists the series
  product check (M_comb against M_LR · M_QZ) as a check beside the constituent
  fits. 0427's only authorized edit is `KitAcceptanceTests.fs`, so the worker
  correctly stopped; no shortcut (fixed object, changed gains, dropped series runs,
  bypassed dispatch) is acceptable.

## Disagreements and additions

1. **Repair criterion.** Stated precisely: a fitted path bearing two or more unknown
   matrices is admitted to the linear engine only when every unknown-bearing item on
   it is also fitted from lone runs in the same stage (structural coverage, as the
   post-mortem says), so the path's rows feed only its series diagnostic. Without
   that coverage, or with a repeated item (double pass) or a coupled/linked product,
   it stays nonlinear; `StudyEngineTests.fs:765-794` must keep passing unchanged.
2. **Supplemental verification is a new gate grant, not a check.** The post-mortem
   adds whole `constructor-unit-tests` and `unit-tests` over
   MuellerReconstructionTests/MuellerInverseTests, neither in `0427.gates`. Under the
   operator's rules these run only if the operator names them. Recommended:
   `constructor-unit-tests` through its own gate (it picks the whole suite,
   `whole_suite: light`), because the repair edits `OpticalConstructor.Optimization`
   and `OpticalConstructor.Tests`. Drop the BerremanTests selection: the repair does
   not touch `MuellerReconstruction.fs` or `MuellerInverse.fs`.
3. **Capture.** The resume reply must also be a committed `.manual/` file with the
   next number, not only text in the ruling (operator rule, 2026-11-14): ruling
   `030-step-0427-series-dispatch-recovery.md`, reply
   `031-step-0427-operator-reply.md`.
4. **First use of the rulings ledger.** `.rulings-jsonl` does not exist; no earlier
   recovery used `rulings_cli`, all relied on `.manual/` files named in the operator
   reply. Either route works; the ledger makes every role at the named steps read
   the ruling automatically. The post-mortem's span `427-494` with the text
   "additional repair authority is confined to 0427" is coherent: later steps read
   it only as a preservation rule. The operator must run it outside any supervisor.

